{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795388894,"nonce":"P7I0NFLLYf6gQ4axKER0ZjSaZ5c=","title":"jno.fem: a boundary term written in the same residual as a volume term is integrated over the volume","message":"Found on feat/fvm. jno.fem([ui.x*vi.x + ui.y*vi.y - 1.0*v.bind(x=xr, y=yr), u(xl, yl) - 0.0]) treats -1.0*v on the right edge as a volume source: the solution is x - x^2/2 (max 0.5) instead of x (max 1). With a coordinate coefficient (-yr*v.bind(...)) the same residual raises \"spans multiple regions\"; with a constant it is silently wrong. Expected: raise, or split the residual by region.","files":null}]}